From 1eb49010f29e984ddb9a2375c64522fbaa90ea7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:57:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 66/66] RDoom 1.1.4: texture eviction without freezes; PB visor
 kept ready

Console (PB + WadFusion, Master Levels, 1.1.3): every texture eviction pass
froze the game for 0.8-1.2 s. The heap sits around 2.3 GB in PB, so a pass
ran every 30 s, and destroying the evicted images costs about 0.23 ms each
(845 ms for 3682 at the start of the next frame).

- Eviction queues the unseen pictures (oldest first) and frees
  rd_vk_texevict_perframe (4) per frame; no GPU wait, no rebuild of every
  texture descriptor set. Pictures that another material also samples (a
  brightmap layer, two textures sharing one picture) are tracked when each
  material is created and keep their GPU copy. Ryujinx: 6065 pictures over
  25 s, heap 1712 -> 1610 MB, no frame over 30 ms (1.1.2: 223-235 ms).
- Big HUD pictures (>= 256x256) are not evicted, and the map-start warm-up
  still loads them (64 MB at most) when the heap is above 1.8 GB: PB's
  radiation suit visor (1472x2160) took 313 ms when picked up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
